      {
        "h_title": "Climate in Ko Samui (Thailand)",
        "main_title": "Climate in Ko Samui (Thailand)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 1,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "In Ko Samui, an island located east of peninsular Thailand, at 9 degrees north latitude, the climate is tropical, hot all year round, with a long rainy season due to the monsoon of Southeast Asia, which runs from May to mid-January, and a drier season from mid-January to April.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "The driest months are February and March, when, however, some showers can sometimes occur.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Temperature",
        "main_title": "Climate in Ko Samui (Thailand)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "As mentioned, the temperature is high throughout the year.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "However, the coolest months are December and January, while from February to May, an increase in temperature is observed, though less marked than in the mainland of Thailand.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "April and May are, albeit slightly, the hottest months.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "In the summer months, the heat continues to be intense and sultry, though tempered by sea breezes, as happens in the rest of the year.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Here are the average temperatures.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
