      {
        "h_title": "Tropical cyclones",
        "main_title": "Climate in Ko Samui (Thailand)",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Koh Samui, like other parts of Thailand, can be affected by tropical cyclones, in particular, by typhoons coming from the east.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "In recent decades, they have entered the Gulf of Thailand only from mid-October to about December 20, although, being the sea always warm, it can not be excluded that they can also be formed in other periods.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Anyway, the Gulf of Thailand is a relatively sheltered area, since it lies halfway between the Bay of Bengal, where cyclones are formed, and the South China Sea, where typhoons arrive from the east, and normally pass to the north, directly affecting the continental part of Thailand.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
